      "severity": "MINOR",
      "title": "Fence scanner's closing-delimiter check does not tolerate a CRLF line ending",
      "file": "shared/scripts/verify.py",
      "line": 1787,
      "profile": "code",
      "disposition": "accepted",
      "reason": "The closing-fence check uses [ \\t]*$, so a CRLF-terminated closing fence would not match and the fence would be treated as unterminated. This is pre-existing rather than introduced here: the earlier single-regex form carried the identical closing check. It is mitigated because .gitattributes enforces LF normalization on text files, so a session log in this repository cannot reach the scanner with CRLF endings. Fixing it would mean widening a checked-in gate's parsing rules outside what this phase changed, with no reachable failure to justify it."
    }
  ],
